exmedetomidine oromucosal gel)</strong> are specifically designed to treat =
noise aversion by calming the dog without heavy sedation. Discuss these opt=
ions with your veterinarian well in advance.</p></li></ul><h4 style=3D"text=
-align: center; white-space: pre-wrap; transition-timing-function: ease; tr=
ansition-duration: 0.8s; transition-delay: 0.258065s;" class=3D"preFade fad=
eIn"><strong>The Owner's Role: Debunking the "Reinforcing Fear" Myth</stron=
g></h4><p class=3D"preFade fadeIn" style=3D"white-space: pre-wrap; transiti=
on-timing-function: ease; transition-duration: 0.8s; transition-delay: 0.26=
129s;"><strong>It is a harmful and outdated myth that comforting a scared d=
og will reinforce their fear.</strong> Fear is an involuntary emotional res=
